## Scoring Rubric

Each query scored on three dimensions, each 0–3. Max per query: **9/9**.

| Dimension | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Factual Grounding (FG)** | Hallucination / fabrication | Some relevant content, multiple key facts missing | Most key facts present, one missing or minor error | All key facts present, every claim traceable to source |
| **SOP Alignment (SOP)** | Contradicts protocol | Partially aligned, key steps missing | Mostly aligned, minor gap | Fully aligned, correct SDMP/DDMP section cited |
| **Appropriate Uncertainty (UNC)** | Confident wrong answer / temporal filter failure | Weak hedge, answer given without valid data | Uncertainty expressed but partial answer given without declining | Correct refusal with explicit reason stated (for IMPACT/CONTAMINATION) OR confident correct answer (for PLANNING/HYBRID pre-event part) |

**Hallucination definition:** A specific factual claim (number, name, figure) not in retrieved
documents but presented with confidence as true. A structured refusal is NOT a hallucination.
Phailin figures presented as Fani figures IS a hallucination.

